{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TCetsAjJXdrHtV3eCRKSBS","type":"tool_result","content":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-07-assigning-the-berth.md:519:One caution, more relevant than it looks: if you use labels for node isolation, choose label keys the kubelet cannot modify. The NodeRestriction admission plugin prevents the kubelet from setting labels with a `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix [source: k8s-docs-assign-pod-node-2026-08-23]. A node that can label itself into a privileged group is not an isolation boundary. The admission gate that enforces this is Chapter 8's *[cross-bearing: see Ch 8 — admission control]*."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a14c5a2b-d3b1-4d5e-aa66-b9d0f14e40bb","uuid":"ffb15c37-0d72-49e8-8ecb-2af80fb00e6b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:41:51.043Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-07-assigning-the-berth.md:519:One caution, more relevant than it looks: if you use labels for node isolation, choose label keys the kubelet cannot modify. The NodeRestriction admission plugin prevents the kubelet from setting labels with a `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix [source: k8s-docs-assign-pod-node-2026-08-23]. A node that can label itself into a privileged group is not an isolation boundary. The admission gate that enforces this is Chapter 8's *[cross-bearing: see Ch 8 — admission control]*.","numLines":1,"totalLines":1}}
